/-!
# Transversal intersections have intersection multiplicity one

Let `A` be a regular local ring with maximal ideal `𝔪`, and let `I`, `J` be two ideals of `A`
satisfying two numerical conditions. The first, `Module.length A (A ⧸ (I ⊔ J)) = 1`, says that the
quotient cut out by both ideals is the residue field: for `A` the local ring of a variety `X` at
the generic point of an irreducible component `Z` of `V ∩ W`, and `I`, `J` the local ideals of two
closed subvarieties `V`, `W`, it says that `Z` occurs with multiplicity one in the closed
subscheme `V ∩ W`. The second, `ringKrullDim A ≤ ringKrullDim (A ⧸ I) + ringKrullDim (A ⧸ J)`, is
the local form of the condition that `V` and `W` intersect properly.

Under these two conditions `I` and `J` are generated by complementary parts of a single regular
system of parameters of `A`. In particular both `A ⧸ I` and `A ⧸ J` are regular local rings, which
is the statement that `V` and `W` are smooth at the general point of `Z`. The Koszul complex of a
generating sequence of `I` then resolves `A ⧸ I` and remains regular after tensoring with `A ⧸ J`,
so `Tor_0^A(A ⧸ I, A ⧸ J)` is the residue field while all higher Tor modules vanish. The
alternating sum of their lengths, which is the intersection multiplicity given by the Tor formula,
is therefore `1`.

## Main definitions

* `Ideal.localIntersectionMultiplicity`: the alternating sum of the lengths of the modules
  `Tor_i^A(A ⧸ I, M)`, the intersection multiplicity computed by the Tor formula.

## Main results

* `IsRegularLocalRing.exists_isRegularSystemOfParameters_of_length_quotient_sup_eq_one`: the two
  ideals are generated by complementary parts of one regular system of parameters, and the
  dimensions of the two quotients are the two lengths.
* `IsRegularLocalRing.isRegularLocalRing_quotient_of_length_quotient_sup_eq_one`: the quotient by
  either of the two ideals is a regular local ring.
* `IsRegularLocalRing.length_tor_quotient_of_length_quotient_sup_eq_one`: the length of
  `Tor_i^A(A ⧸ I, A ⧸ J)` is `1` for `i = 0` and `0` otherwise.
* `IsRegularLocalRing.localIntersectionMultiplicity_eq_one_of_length_quotient_sup_eq_one`: the
  Tor-formula intersection multiplicity of the pair is `1`.

## Implementation notes

The multiplicity is an unbounded alternating sum, written as a `tsum` over `ℕ`; over a regular
local ring all but finitely many terms vanish, and the main computation pins every individual
term, so no truncation has to be chosen.

Dimensions take values in `WithBot ℕ∞`, which has no subtraction, so the dimension count is
transported to `ℕ` through `(·.unbotD 0).toNat`, legitimate because a Noetherian local ring has
finite nonnegative dimension. The count itself compares three quantities: the dimension of the
image of an ideal in the cotangent space `𝔪 / 𝔪²` plus the dimension of the quotient by that
ideal is at most the dimension of the ring; the two cotangent images span the cotangent space,
because the two ideals generate `𝔪`; and proper intersection bounds the dimension of the ring by
the sum of the dimensions of the two quotients. Together these force equality everywhere, which
is what makes both quotients regular.

Tor is Mathlib's derived tensor product on `ModuleCat`, derived in the second variable; the
Koszul resolution of `A ⧸ I` computes it through the balancing isomorphism `Tor ≅ Tor'`, and
degree zero is read off from the right exactness of the tensor product instead.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B1I](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B1I)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AZR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AZR)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits IsLocalRing
open scoped ExteriorAlgebra TensorProduct
open Stacks.RegularLocalRing.RegularQuotient (cotangentImage mem_cotangentImage_iff
  eq_of_le_of_ringKrullDim_quotient_eq)

universe u

/-- The **intersection multiplicity computed by the Tor formula**: for an ideal `I` of a ring `A`
and an `A`-module `M`, the alternating sum `∑ (-1)^i length_A Tor_i^A(A ⧸ I, M)`. When `A` is the
local ring of a nonsingular variety `X` at the generic point of an irreducible component `Z` of
`V ∩ W`, with `I` the local ideal of `V` and `M` the local ring of `W`, this is the intersection
multiplicity `e(X, V · W, Z)`. -/
@[sga "4½ Cycle 2.3.9", sga "4½ Cycle 3.5"]
def Ideal.localIntersectionMultiplicity {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A)
    (M : Type u) [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M] : ℚ :=
  ∑' i : ℕ, (-1 : ℚ) ^ i *
    ((Module.length A
      (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I))).obj
        (ModuleCat.of A M))).toNat : ℚ)

namespace IsRegularLocalRing

/-! ### The image of an ideal in the cotangent space -/

/-- Two ideals generating the maximal ideal have cotangent images spanning the cotangent
space. -/
private lemma cotImage_sup_eq_top {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    (I J : Ideal R) (hI : I ≤ maximalIdeal R) (hJ : J ≤ maximalIdeal R)
    (hsum : I ⊔ J = maximalIdeal R) : cotangentImage I ⊔ cotangentImage J = ⊤ := by
  refine eq_top_iff.mpr fun v _ => ?_
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := (maximalIdeal R).toCotangent_surjective v
  have hx : (x : R) ∈ I ⊔ J := by
    rw [hsum]
    exact x.2
  obtain ⟨a, ha, b, hb, hab⟩ := Submodule.mem_sup.mp hx
  rw [show x = ⟨a, hI ha⟩ + ⟨b, hJ hb⟩ from Subtype.ext hab.symm, map_add]
  exact add_mem (Submodule.mem_sup_left (mem_cotangentImage_iff.mpr ⟨⟨a, hI ha⟩, ha, rfl⟩))
    (Submodule.mem_sup_right (mem_cotangentImage_iff.mpr ⟨⟨b, hJ hb⟩, hb, rfl⟩))

/-! ### Regular systems of parameters -/

/-- The underlying elements of a concatenated family in the maximal ideal are the concatenation
of the underlying elements. -/
private lemma val_comp_append {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] {a b : ℕ}
    (f : Fin a → maximalIdeal R) (g : Fin b → maximalIdeal R) :
    (fun i : Fin (a + b) => ((Fin.append f g i : maximalIdeal R) : R)) =
      Fin.append (fun i : Fin a => (f i : R)) (fun j : Fin b => (g j : R)) := by
  funext i
  refine Fin.addCases (fun i => ?_) (fun j => ?_) i <;> simp [Fin.append]

/-- The cotangent classes of a concatenated family range over the union of the two ranges. -/
private lemma range_toCotangent_append {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] {a b : ℕ}
    (f : Fin a → maximalIdeal R) (g : Fin b → maximalIdeal R) :
    Set.range (fun i : Fin (a + b) => (maximalIdeal R).toCotangent (Fin.append f g i)) =
      Set.range (fun i : Fin a => (maximalIdeal R).toCotangent (f i)) ∪
        Set.range (fun j : Fin b => (maximalIdeal R).toCotangent (g j)) := by
  ext w
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨i, rfl⟩
    refine Fin.addCases (fun i => ?_) (fun j => ?_) i
    · exact Or.inl ⟨i, by simp [Fin.append]⟩
    · exact Or.inr ⟨j, by simp [Fin.append]⟩
  · rintro (⟨i, rfl⟩ | ⟨j, rfl⟩)
    · exact ⟨Fin.castAdd b i, by simp [Fin.append]⟩
    · exact ⟨Fin.natAdd a j, by simp [Fin.append]⟩

/-- A regular system of parameters generates the maximal ideal and has the minimal possible
length. -/
@[sga "2 IV 5.3" "partial"]
private lemma isRegularSystemOfParameters_generates {R : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [IsRegularLocalRing R] {n : ℕ} (y : Fin n → maximalIdeal R)
    (h : IsRegularSystemOfParameters y) :
    Ideal.ofList (List.ofFn fun i => (y i : R)) = maximalIdeal R ∧
      (List.ofFn fun i => (y i : R)).length = (maximalIdeal R).spanFinrank := by
  have hcot : Submodule.span (ResidueField R)
      ((maximalIdeal R).toCotangent '' Set.range y) = ⊤ := by
    simpa [← Set.range_comp'] using h.2
  refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [Ideal.ofList_ofFn]
    calc
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => (y i : R))
          = Submodule.map (maximalIdeal R).subtype (Submodule.span R (Set.range y)) := by
            rw [Submodule.map_span, ← Set.range_comp]
            rfl
      _ = maximalIdeal R := by
        rw [CotangentSpace.span_image_eq_top_iff.mp hcot, Submodule.map_top,
          Submodule.range_subtype]
  · rw [List.length_ofFn, spanFinrank_maximalIdeal_eq_finrank_cotangentSpace]
    simpa using (Module.finrank_eq_card_basis (Module.Basis.mk h.1 (by rw [h.2]))).symm

/-- **The initial part of a regular system of parameters.** It is a regular sequence, the ideal it
generates has a regular local quotient, and the dimension of that quotient drops by its
length. -/
@[ega "0 17.1.7" "a⇒b", ega "0 17.1.9" "(b) ⇒ (a)"]
private lemma isRegularSystemOfParameters_take {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsRegularLocalRing R]
    {a b : ℕ} (f : Fin a → maximalIdeal R) (g : Fin b → maximalIdeal R)
    (h : IsRegularSystemOfParameters (Fin.append f g)) :
    RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular R (List.ofFn fun i : Fin a => (f i : R)) ∧
      IsRegularLocalRing (R ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range fun i : Fin a => (f i : R))) ∧
      ringKrullDim (R ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range fun i : Fin a => (f i : R))) + a =
        ringKrullDim R := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨hspan, hlen⟩ := isRegularSystemOfParameters_generates _ h
  set xs : List R := List.ofFn fun i : Fin (a + b) => ((Fin.append f g i : maximalIdeal R) : R)
    with hxs
  have hsplit : xs = List.ofFn (fun i : Fin a => (f i : R)) ++
      List.ofFn (fun j : Fin b => (g j : R)) := by
    rw [hxs, val_comp_append f g, List.ofFn_fin_append]
  obtain ⟨hregxs, hquot⟩ :=
    (IsRegularLocalRing.isRegular_and_isRegularLocalRing_quotient_and_isMaximalCohenMacaulay
      R).1 xs hspan hlen
  have hprefix : Ideal.ofList (xs.take a) =
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun i : Fin a => (f i : R)) := by
    rw [hsplit, List.take_append_of_le_length (by simp), List.take_of_length_le (by simp),
      Ideal.ofList_ofFn]
  have hdata := hquot a (by simp [hxs])
  rw [hprefix] at hdata
  refine ⟨?_, hdata.1, hdata.2⟩
  have hweak : RingTheory.Sequence.IsWeaklyRegular R
      (List.ofFn (fun i : Fin a => (f i : R)) ++ List.ofFn (fun j : Fin b => (g j : R))) := by
    rw [← hsplit]
    exact hregxs.toIsWeaklyRegular
  refine RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular.of_isWeaklyRegular_of_mem_maximalIdeal R ?_
    ((RingTheory.Sequence.isWeaklyRegular_append_iff R _ _).mp hweak).1
  intro r hr
  obtain ⟨i, rfl⟩ := List.mem_ofFn.mp hr
  exact (f i).property

/-! ### Extending a linearly independent family to a spanning family -/

/-- A linearly independent family in a finite-dimensional vector space can be completed by
`finrank - n` further vectors to a spanning family. -/
private lemma exists_spanning_completion {K V : Type*} [DivisionRing K] [AddCommGroup V]
    [Module K V] [FiniteDimensional K V] {n : ℕ} {a : Fin n → V}
    (ha : LinearIndependent K a) :
    ∃ b : Fin (Module.finrank K V - n) → V,
      Submodule.span K (Set.range a ∪ Set.range b) = ⊤ := by
  classical
  set W := Submodule.span K (Set.range a) with hW
  have hq : Module.finrank K (V ⧸ W) = Module.finrank K V - n := by
    have h1 : Module.finrank K W = n := by
      rw [hW, finrank_span_eq_card ha, Fintype.card_fin]
    have := Submodule.finrank_quotient_add_finrank W
    omega
  set B := (Module.finBasis K (V ⧸ W)).reindex (finCongr hq)
  set b : Fin (Module.finrank K V - n) → V :=
    fun j => Function.surjInv W.mkQ_surjective (B j)
  have hmap : (Submodule.span K (Set.range a ∪ Set.range b)).map W.mkQ = ⊤ := by
    rw [Submodule.map_span]
    refine top_le_iff.mp (B.span_eq.ge.trans (Submodule.span_mono ?_))
    rintro _ ⟨j, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨b j, Or.inr ⟨j, rfl⟩, Function.surjInv_eq _ _⟩
  have hker : LinearMap.ker W.mkQ ≤ Submodule.span K (Set.range a ∪ Set.range b) := by
    rw [Submodule.ker_mkQ]
    exact Submodule.span_mono Set.subset_union_left
  have h := Submodule.comap_map_eq_self hker
  rw [hmap, Submodule.comap_top] at h
  exact ⟨b, h.symm⟩

/-- A family in `𝔪` of length `dim 𝔪 / 𝔪²` whose cotangent classes span is a regular system of
parameters. -/
private lemma isRegularSystemOfParameters_append_of_span_eq_top {R : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [IsRegularLocalRing R] {a b : ℕ} (f : Fin a → maximalIdeal R) (g : Fin b → maximalIdeal R)
    (hspan : Submodule.span (ResidueField R) (Set.range (fun i : Fin (a + b) =>
      (maximalIdeal R).toCotangent (Fin.append f g i))) = ⊤)
    (hcard : a + b = Module.finrank (ResidueField R) (CotangentSpace R)) :
    IsRegularSystemOfParameters (Fin.append f g) :=
  ⟨linearIndependent_of_top_le_span_of_card_eq_finrank (R := ResidueField R) hspan.ge
    (by rw [Fintype.card_fin, hcard]), hspan⟩

/-- A family in `𝔪` whose cotangent classes are linearly independent is the initial part of a
regular system of parameters. -/
private lemma exists_append_isRegularSystemOfParameters {R : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [IsRegularLocalRing R] {c : ℕ} (f : Fin c → maximalIdeal R)
    (hli : LinearIndependent (ResidueField R)
      (fun i => (maximalIdeal R).toCotangent (f i))) :
    ∃ g : Fin (Module.finrank (ResidueField R) (CotangentSpace R) - c) → maximalIdeal R,
      IsRegularSystemOfParameters (Fin.append f g) := by
  classical
  set d := Module.finrank (ResidueField R) (CotangentSpace R) with hd
  have hc : c ≤ d := by simpa [hd, Fintype.card_fin] using hli.fintype_card_le_finrank
  obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := exists_spanning_completion hli
  choose g hg using fun j : Fin (d - c) => (maximalIdeal R).toCotangent_surjective (w j)
  have hgrange : Set.range (fun j : Fin (d - c) =>
      (maximalIdeal R).toCotangent (g j)) = Set.range w :=
    congrArg Set.range (funext hg)
  refine ⟨g, isRegularSystemOfParameters_append_of_span_eq_top f g ?_ (by omega)⟩
  rw [range_toCotangent_append f g, hgrange]
  exact hw

/-! ### Dimension bookkeeping -/

/-- The Krull dimension of a Noetherian local ring is the cast of a natural number. -/
private lemma ringKrullDim_eq_natCast_unbotD_toNat {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    [IsLocalRing R] : ringKrullDim R = ((ringKrullDim R).unbotD 0).toNat := by
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ :=
    Stacks.RegularLocalRing.KernelRegularity.exists_natCast_eq_ringKrullDim R
  rw [hn]
  simp

/-- An ideal of a local ring whose quotient has length one is the maximal ideal. -/
private lemma eq_maximalIdeal_of_length_quotient_eq_one {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R]
    (I : Ideal R) (h : Module.length R (R ⧸ I) = 1) : I = maximalIdeal R := by
  have hs : IsSimpleModule R (R ⧸ I) := Module.length_eq_one_iff.mp h
  have hmax : (Module.annihilator R (R ⧸ I)).IsMaximal := IsSimpleModule.annihilator_isMaximal
  rw [Ideal.annihilator_quotient] at hmax
  exact IsLocalRing.eq_maximalIdeal hmax

/-- The quotient of a local ring by a proper ideal is a nontrivial local ring. -/
private lemma nontrivial_and_isLocalRing_quotient {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R]
    {I : Ideal R} (hI : I ≤ maximalIdeal R) : Nontrivial (R ⧸ I) ∧ IsLocalRing (R ⧸ I) :=
  have : Nontrivial (R ⧸ I) := Ideal.Quotient.nontrivial_iff.mpr fun h =>
    (maximalIdeal.isMaximal R).ne_top (top_le_iff.mp (h ▸ hI))
  ⟨this, IsLocalRing.of_surjective' (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective⟩

/-- The Krull dimension of the quotient of a Noetherian local ring by a proper ideal is the cast of
a natural number. -/
private lemma ringKrullDim_quotient_eq_natCast_unbotD_toNat {R : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsLocalRing R] {I : Ideal R} (hI : I ≤ maximalIdeal R) :
    ringKrullDim (R ⧸ I) = ((ringKrullDim (R ⧸ I)).unbotD 0).toNat := by
  obtain ⟨_, _⟩ := nontrivial_and_isLocalRing_quotient hI
  have : IsNoetherianRing (R ⧸ I) :=
    isNoetherianRing_of_surjective R (R ⧸ I) (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  exact ringKrullDim_eq_natCast_unbotD_toNat

/-- A basis of the cotangent image of an ideal lifts to a family of elements of the ideal. -/
private lemma exists_toCotangent_lift_of_cotangentImage {R : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [IsRegularLocalRing R] (I : Ideal R) :
    ∃ f : Fin (Module.finrank (ResidueField R) (cotangentImage I)) → maximalIdeal R,
      (∀ i, (f i : R) ∈ I) ∧
      LinearIndependent (ResidueField R) (fun i => (maximalIdeal R).toCotangent (f i)) ∧
      Submodule.span (ResidueField R)
        (Set.range fun i => (maximalIdeal R).toCotangent (f i)) = cotangentImage I := by
  classical
  set B := Module.finBasis (ResidueField R) (cotangentImage I)
  choose f hfmem hfclass using fun i => mem_cotangentImage_iff.mp (B i).property
  have hfun : (fun i => (maximalIdeal R).toCotangent (f i)) = (cotangentImage I).subtype ∘ B :=
    funext fun i => hfclass i
  refine ⟨f, hfmem, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [hfun]
    exact B.linearIndependent.map' (cotangentImage I).subtype
      (LinearMap.ker_eq_bot'.mpr fun x hx => Subtype.ext hx)
  · rw [hfun, Set.range_comp, ← Submodule.map_span, B.span_eq, Submodule.map_top,
      Submodule.range_subtype]

/-- The dimension of the cotangent image of an ideal plus the dimension of the quotient by that
ideal is at most the dimension of the ring. -/
private lemma finrank_cotImage_add_ringKrullDim_quotient_le {R : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [IsRegularLocalRing R] (I : Ideal R) :
    (Module.finrank (ResidueField R) (cotangentImage I) : WithBot ℕ∞) + ringKrullDim (R ⧸ I) ≤
      ringKrullDim R := by
  classical
  set c := Module.finrank (ResidueField R) (cotangentImage I)
  obtain ⟨f, hfmem, hli, -⟩ := exists_toCotangent_lift_of_cotangentImage I
  obtain ⟨g, hparam⟩ := exists_append_isRegularSystemOfParameters f hli
  set K : Ideal R := Ideal.span (Set.range fun i : Fin c => (f i : R))
  have hKI : K ≤ I := Ideal.span_le.mpr (Set.range_subset_iff.mpr hfmem)
  have hdimle : ringKrullDim (R ⧸ I) ≤ ringKrullDim (R ⧸ K) :=
    ringKrullDim_le_of_surjective (Ideal.Quotient.factor hKI)
      (Ideal.Quotient.factor_surjective hKI)
  calc
    (c : WithBot ℕ∞) + ringKrullDim (R ⧸ I) ≤ (c : WithBot ℕ∞) + ringKrullDim (R ⧸ K) :=
      add_le_add_right hdimle _
    _ = ringKrullDim (R ⧸ K) + (c : WithBot ℕ∞) := add_comm _ _
    _ = ringKrullDim R := (isRegularSystemOfParameters_take f g hparam).2.2

/-- An ideal containing the initial part of a regular system of parameters, whose quotient has
the dimension of the final part, is generated by the initial part. -/
private lemma eq_span_of_isRegularSystemOfParameters_append {R : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [IsRegularLocalRing R] {a b : ℕ} {f : Fin a → maximalIdeal R} {g : Fin b → maximalIdeal R}
    (h : IsRegularSystemOfParameters (Fin.append f g)) {I : Ideal R} (hf : ∀ i, (f i : R) ∈ I)
    (hdim : ringKrullDim (R ⧸ I) = (b : WithBot ℕ∞)) :
    I = Ideal.span (Set.range fun i : Fin a => (f i : R)) := by
  have hdimR : ringKrullDim R = ((a + b : ℕ) : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
    rw [← IsRegularLocalRing.spanFinrank_maximalIdeal (R := R),
      ← (isRegularSystemOfParameters_generates _ h).2, List.length_ofFn]
  set K : Ideal R := Ideal.span (Set.range fun i : Fin a => (f i : R))
  have hKle : K ≤ I := Ideal.span_le.mpr (Set.range_subset_iff.mpr hf)
  have hQ := isRegularSystemOfParameters_take f g h
  have : IsRegularLocalRing (R ⧸ K) := hQ.2.1
  have : IsDomain (R ⧸ K) := IsRegularLocalRing.isDomain (R ⧸ K)
  have hKcast : ringKrullDim (R ⧸ K) =
      (((ringKrullDim (R ⧸ K)).unbotD 0).toNat : WithBot ℕ∞) :=
    ringKrullDim_eq_natCast_unbotD_toNat
  have hnat : ((ringKrullDim (R ⧸ K)).unbotD 0).toNat + a = a + b := by
    have h' := hQ.2.2
    rw [hKcast, hdimR] at h'
    exact_mod_cast h'
  have hKdim : ringKrullDim (R ⧸ K) = (b : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
    rw [hKcast, show ((ringKrullDim (R ⧸ K)).unbotD 0).toNat = b by omega]
  exact (eq_of_le_of_ringKrullDim_quotient_eq hKle hKdim hdim).symm

/-! ### The structure of a transversal pair of ideals -/

/-- **Transversal ideals are generated by complementary parameters.** Let `A` be a regular local
ring and let `I`, `J` be ideals such that `A ⧸ (I ⊔ J)` has length one and
`dim A ≤ dim (A ⧸ I) + dim (A ⧸ J)`. Then there is a regular system of parameters of `A`, split
into an initial part of length `a` generating `I` and a final part of length `b` generating `J`,
and the two quotients have dimensions `b` and `a`. -/
theorem exists_isRegularSystemOfParameters_of_length_quotient_sup_eq_one {A : Type u} [CommRing A]
    [IsRegularLocalRing A] (I J : Ideal A) (hmult : Module.length A (A ⧸ (I ⊔ J)) = 1)
    (hproper : ringKrullDim A ≤ ringKrullDim (A ⧸ I) + ringKrullDim (A ⧸ J)) :
    ∃ (a b : ℕ) (f : Fin a → maximalIdeal A) (g : Fin b → maximalIdeal A),
      IsRegularSystemOfParameters (Fin.append f g) ∧
      I = Ideal.span (Set.range fun i : Fin a => (f i : A)) ∧
      J = Ideal.span (Set.range fun j : Fin b => (g j : A)) ∧
      ringKrullDim (A ⧸ I) = (b : WithBot ℕ∞) ∧ ringKrullDim (A ⧸ J) = (a : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  classical
  have hsum : I ⊔ J = maximalIdeal A := eq_maximalIdeal_of_length_quotient_eq_one _ hmult
  have hIle : I ≤ maximalIdeal A := le_sup_left.trans hsum.le
  have hJle : J ≤ maximalIdeal A := le_sup_right.trans hsum.le
  set dA : ℕ := ((ringKrullDim A).unbotD 0).toNat
  set dI : ℕ := ((ringKrullDim (A ⧸ I)).unbotD 0).toNat
  set dJ : ℕ := ((ringKrullDim (A ⧸ J)).unbotD 0).toNat
  have hAcast : ringKrullDim A = (dA : WithBot ℕ∞) := ringKrullDim_eq_natCast_unbotD_toNat
  have hIcast : ringKrullDim (A ⧸ I) = (dI : WithBot ℕ∞) :=
    ringKrullDim_quotient_eq_natCast_unbotD_toNat hIle
  have hJcast : ringKrullDim (A ⧸ J) = (dJ : WithBot ℕ∞) :=
    ringKrullDim_quotient_eq_natCast_unbotD_toNat hJle
  set a : ℕ := Module.finrank (ResidueField A) (cotangentImage I) with ha
  set b : ℕ := Module.finrank (ResidueField A) (cotangentImage J) with hb
  obtain ⟨f, hfmem, -, hspanI⟩ := exists_toCotangent_lift_of_cotangentImage I
  obtain ⟨g, hgmem, -, hspanJ⟩ := exists_toCotangent_lift_of_cotangentImage J
  have hcot : ∀ (K : Ideal A) (d : ℕ), ringKrullDim (A ⧸ K) = (d : WithBot ℕ∞) →
      Module.finrank (ResidueField A) (cotangentImage K) + d ≤ dA := fun K d hd => by
    have h := finrank_cotImage_add_ringKrullDim_quotient_le (R := A) K
    rw [hd, hAcast] at h
    exact_mod_cast h
  have hcotI : a + dI ≤ dA := hcot I dI hIcast
  have hcotJ : b + dJ ≤ dA := hcot J dJ hJcast
  have hproperNat : dA ≤ dI + dJ := by
    rw [hAcast, hIcast, hJcast] at hproper
    exact_mod_cast hproper
  have hcotDim : Module.finrank (ResidueField A) (CotangentSpace A) = dA := by
    have h : (Module.finrank (ResidueField A) (CotangentSpace A) : WithBot ℕ∞) =
        (dA : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
      rw [← spanFinrank_maximalIdeal_eq_finrank_cotangentSpace,
        IsRegularLocalRing.spanFinrank_maximalIdeal, hAcast]
    exact_mod_cast h
  have hspan := cotImage_sup_eq_top I J hIle hJle hsum
  have hsumFin : dA ≤ a + b := by
    have h := Submodule.finrank_add_le_finrank_add_finrank (cotangentImage I) (cotangentImage J)
    rwa [hspan, finrank_top, hcotDim] at h
  have hparam := isRegularSystemOfParameters_append_of_span_eq_top f g
    (by rw [range_toCotangent_append f g, Submodule.span_union, hspanI, hspanJ, hspan])
    (by rw [← ha, ← hb]; omega)
  have hparamSwap := isRegularSystemOfParameters_append_of_span_eq_top g f
    (by rw [range_toCotangent_append g f, Submodule.span_union, hspanI, hspanJ, sup_comm, hspan])
    (by rw [← ha, ← hb]; omega)
  have hdimI : ringKrullDim (A ⧸ I) = (b : WithBot ℕ∞) := by rw [hIcast, show dI = b by omega]
  have hdimJ : ringKrullDim (A ⧸ J) = (a : WithBot ℕ∞) := by rw [hJcast, show dJ = a by omega]
  exact ⟨a, b, f, g, hparam, eq_span_of_isRegularSystemOfParameters_append hparam hfmem hdimI,
    eq_span_of_isRegularSystemOfParameters_append hparamSwap hgmem hdimJ, hdimI, hdimJ⟩

/-- **Both quotients are regular.** At a transversal pair of ideals of a regular local ring the
quotient by the first ideal is again a regular local ring. Geometrically: two closed subvarieties
intersecting properly along a component of multiplicity one are smooth at the general point of
that component. -/
theorem isRegularLocalRing_quotient_of_length_quotient_sup_eq_one {A : Type u} [CommRing A]
    [IsRegularLocalRing A] (I J : Ideal A) (hmult : Module.length A (A ⧸ (I ⊔ J)) = 1)
    (hproper : ringKrullDim A ≤ ringKrullDim (A ⧸ I) + ringKrullDim (A ⧸ J)) :
    IsRegularLocalRing (A ⧸ I) := by
  obtain ⟨a, b, f, g, hparam, hI, -, -, -⟩ :=
    exists_isRegularSystemOfParameters_of_length_quotient_sup_eq_one I J hmult hproper
  rw [hI]
  exact (isRegularSystemOfParameters_take f g hparam).2.1

/-- **A transversal pair of ideals meets in the expected dimension.** At a pair of ideals of a
regular local ring `A` with `A ⧸ (I ⊔ J)` of length one and
`dim A ≤ dim (A ⧸ I) + dim (A ⧸ J)`, the inequality is an equality: the two ideals are generated
by complementary parts of one regular system of parameters, whose length is `dim A`. -/
theorem ringKrullDim_eq_add_of_length_quotient_sup_eq_one {A : Type u} [CommRing A]
    [IsRegularLocalRing A] (I J : Ideal A) (hmult : Module.length A (A ⧸ (I ⊔ J)) = 1)
    (hproper : ringKrullDim A ≤ ringKrullDim (A ⧸ I) + ringKrullDim (A ⧸ J)) :
    ringKrullDim A = ringKrullDim (A ⧸ I) + ringKrullDim (A ⧸ J) := by
  obtain ⟨a, b, f, g, hparam, hI, -, hdI, hdJ⟩ :=
    exists_isRegularSystemOfParameters_of_length_quotient_sup_eq_one I J hmult hproper
  have h := (isRegularSystemOfParameters_take f g hparam).2.2
  rw [← hI] at h
  rw [← h, hdJ]

/-! ### Computing the Tor modules -/

/-- The Koszul complex of a regular sequence, with its augmentation, is a projective resolution
of the quotient by the ideal the sequence generates. -/
@[sga "6 VII 1.1" "special case", sga "6 VIII 1.4" "affine case"]
private def koszulResolution {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → A)
    (hf : RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular A (List.ofFn f)) :
    ProjectiveResolution (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range f))) :=
  have hreg : Koszul.IsKoszulRegular f :=
    (Koszul.isKoszulRegularOn_and_isKoszulRegular_of_regular (M := A)).2.2 hf
  { complex := Koszul.seqComplex f
    projective := fun n => ModuleCat.projective_of_free ((Pi.basisFun A (Fin r)).exteriorPower n)
    π := Koszul.koszulAugmentation f
    quasiIso := Koszul.koszulAugmentation_quasiIso f hreg }

/-- Tor against the quotient by a regular sequence is the homology of the Koszul complex with
coefficients. -/
private def torIsoKoszulHomology {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → A)
    (hf : RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular A (List.ofFn f)) (I : Ideal A)
    (hI : I = Ideal.span (Set.range f)) (M : Type u) [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M] (i : ℕ) :
    (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I))).obj (ModuleCat.of A M)) ≅
      ModuleCat.of A ((Koszul.seqComplexTensor f M).homology i) := by
  subst I
  let P := koszulResolution f hf
  let e₁ := (Tor_iso_Tor' A i).app (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range f)))
  let e₂ := P.isoLeftDerivedObj
    ((CategoryTheory.MonoidalCategory.tensoringRight (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj
      (ModuleCat.of A M)) i
  have hC : (((CategoryTheory.MonoidalCategory.tensoringRight (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj
      (ModuleCat.of A M)).mapHomologicalComplex (ComplexShape.down ℕ)).obj
        (Koszul.seqComplex f) = Koszul.seqComplexTensor f M := by
    unfold Koszul.seqComplex Koszul.complex Koszul.seqComplexTensor
    rw [ChainComplex.map_chain_complex_of]
    rfl
  simpa [Tor', CategoryTheory.MonoidalCategory.tensoringRight,
    HomologicalComplex.homologyFunctor, P, koszulResolution, hC] using
      e₁.app (ModuleCat.of A M) ≪≫ e₂

/-- Tor in degree zero is the tensor product, by right exactness. -/
private def torZeroIsoTensor {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (X Y : ModuleCat.{u} A) :
    ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) 0).obj X).obj Y ≅ ModuleCat.of A (X ⊗[A] Y) :=
  (((CategoryTheory.MonoidalCategory.tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj
    X).leftDerivedZeroIsoSelf).app Y

/-- The tensor product of two cyclic modules is the quotient by the sum of the two ideals. -/
@[ega "IV 11.7.5" "partial"]
private def quotTensorQuotEquiv {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (I J : Ideal A) :
    ((A ⧸ I) ⊗[A] (A ⧸ J)) ≃ₗ[A] A ⧸ (I ⊔ J) := by
  have hmap : Submodule.map (Submodule.mkQ (J : Submodule A A)) I =
      I • (⊤ : Submodule A (A ⧸ J)) := by
    calc
      Submodule.map (Submodule.mkQ (J : Submodule A A)) I =
          Submodule.map (Submodule.mkQ J) (I • (⊤ : Submodule A A)) := by
            congr 1
            ext x
            simp
      _ = I • Submodule.map (Submodule.mkQ J) (⊤ : Submodule A A) := Submodule.map_smul'' I _ _
      _ = I • (⊤ : Submodule A (A ⧸ J)) := by simp [Submodule.range_mkQ]
  have hsup : (J : Submodule A A) ⊔ (I : Submodule A A) = ((I ⊔ J : Ideal A) : Submodule A A) :=
    sup_comm _ _
  exact (TensorProduct.quotTensorEquivQuotSMul (A ⧸ J) I).trans
    (((Submodule.quotEquivOfEq _ _ hmap.symm).trans
      (Submodule.quotientQuotientEquivQuotientSup (J : Submodule A A)
        (I : Submodule A A))).trans (Submodule.quotEquivOfEq _ _ hsup))

/-- **Degree zero of the Tor formula at two cyclic modules.** The length of
`Tor_0^A(A ⧸ I, A ⧸ J)` is the length of `A ⧸ (I ⊔ J)`: degree zero of Tor is the tensor
product, by right exactness, and the tensor product of two cyclic modules is the quotient by the
sum of the two ideals. -/
theorem length_tor_zero_quotient_eq {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (I J : Ideal A) :
    Module.length A
        (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) 0).obj (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I))).obj
          (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ J))) = Module.length A (A ⧸ (I ⊔ J)) := by
  rw [(torZeroIsoTensor (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I))
      (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ J))).toLinearEquiv.length_eq, (quotTensorQuotEquiv I J).length_eq]

/-- At a transversal pair of ideals of a regular local ring, generators of the first ideal coming
from a regular system of parameters form a weakly regular sequence on the quotient by the
second. -/
private lemma isWeaklyRegular_quotient_of_length_quotient_sup_eq_one {A : Type u} [CommRing A]
    [IsRegularLocalRing A] (I J : Ideal A) (hmult : Module.length A (A ⧸ (I ⊔ J)) = 1)
    (hproper : ringKrullDim A ≤ ringKrullDim (A ⧸ I) + ringKrullDim (A ⧸ J)) {a : ℕ}
    {f : Fin a → maximalIdeal A} (hI : I = Ideal.span (Set.range fun i : Fin a => (f i : A)))
    (hdimJ : ringKrullDim (A ⧸ J) = (a : WithBot ℕ∞)) :
    RingTheory.Sequence.IsWeaklyRegular (A ⧸ J) (List.ofFn fun i : Fin a => (f i : A)) := by
  classical
  have hsum : I ⊔ J = maximalIdeal A := eq_maximalIdeal_of_length_quotient_eq_one _ hmult
  obtain ⟨_, _⟩ := nontrivial_and_isLocalRing_quotient (le_sup_right.trans hsum.le)
  have hregJ : IsRegularLocalRing (A ⧸ J) :=
    isRegularLocalRing_quotient_of_length_quotient_sup_eq_one J I
      (by rwa [sup_comm]) (by rwa [add_comm])
  have hspanfb : Ideal.span (Set.range fun i : Fin a =>
      Ideal.Quotient.mk J (f i : A)) = maximalIdeal (A ⧸ J) := by
    calc
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun i : Fin a => Ideal.Quotient.mk J (f i : A))
          = Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) I := by
            rw [hI, Ideal.map_span, ← Set.range_comp]
            rfl
      _ = Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) (I ⊔ J) := by
            rw [Ideal.map_sup, Ideal.map_quotient_self, sup_bot_eq]
      _ = Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) (maximalIdeal A) := congrArg _ hsum
      _ = maximalIdeal (A ⧸ J) :=
            IsLocalRing.map_maximalIdeal_of_surjective _ Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  have hlenfb : (List.ofFn fun i : Fin a => Ideal.Quotient.mk J (f i : A)).length =
      (maximalIdeal (A ⧸ J)).spanFinrank := by
    simp only [List.length_ofFn]
    have hcast : ((maximalIdeal (A ⧸ J)).spanFinrank : WithBot ℕ∞) = (a : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
      rw [hregJ.spanFinrank_maximalIdeal]
      exact hdimJ
    exact_mod_cast hcast.symm
  have := hregJ
  obtain ⟨hregfb, -⟩ :=
    (IsRegularLocalRing.isRegular_and_isRegularLocalRing_quotient_and_isMaximalCohenMacaulay
      (A ⧸ J)).1 (List.ofFn fun i : Fin a => Ideal.Quotient.mk J (f i : A))
        (by rwa [Ideal.ofList_ofFn]) hlenfb
  have hmapeq : (List.ofFn fun i : Fin a => (f i : A)).map (algebraMap A (A ⧸ J)) =
      List.ofFn fun i : Fin a => Ideal.Quotient.mk J (f i : A) := by
    rw [List.map_ofFn, Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_eq]
    rfl
  refine (RingTheory.Sequence.isWeaklyRegular_map_algebraMap_iff (A ⧸ J) (A ⧸ J)
      (List.ofFn fun i : Fin a => (f i : A))).mp ?_
  rw [hmapeq]
  exact hregfb.toIsWeaklyRegular

/-- **The Tor modules of a transversal pair.** At a transversal pair of ideals of a regular local
ring, `Tor_0^A(A ⧸ I, A ⧸ J)` is the residue field and all higher Tor modules vanish: the length
of `Tor_i^A(A ⧸ I, A ⧸ J)` is `1` for `i = 0` and `0` otherwise. -/
theorem length_tor_quotient_of_length_quotient_sup_eq_one {A : Type u} [CommRing A]
    [IsRegularLocalRing A] (I J : Ideal A) (hmult : Module.length A (A ⧸ (I ⊔ J)) = 1)
    (hproper : ringKrullDim A ≤ ringKrullDim (A ⧸ I) + ringKrullDim (A ⧸ J)) (i : ℕ) :
    Module.length A
        (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I))).obj
          (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ J))) = if i = 0 then 1 else 0 := by
  classical
  by_cases hi : i = 0
  · subst hi
    rw [if_pos rfl, length_tor_zero_quotient_eq, hmult]
  · rw [if_neg hi]
    obtain ⟨a, b, f, g, hparam, hI, -, -, hdimJ⟩ :=
      exists_isRegularSystemOfParameters_of_length_quotient_sup_eq_one I J hmult hproper
    refine ((torIsoKoszulHomology _ (isRegularSystemOfParameters_take f g hparam).1 I hI
      (A ⧸ J) i).toLinearEquiv.length_eq).trans (Module.length_eq_zero_iff.mpr
        (ModuleCat.isZero_iff_subsingleton.mp ?_))
    exact (Koszul.isKoszulRegularOn_and_isKoszulRegular_of_regular (M := A ⧸ J)).1
      (isWeaklyRegular_quotient_of_length_quotient_sup_eq_one I J hmult hproper hI hdimJ) i hi

/-- **Stacks 0B1I, the multiplicity-one case of the Tor formula.** Let `A` be a regular local ring
and let `I`, `J` be ideals with `Module.length A (A ⧸ (I ⊔ J)) = 1` and
`dim A ≤ dim (A ⧸ I) + dim (A ⧸ J)`. Then the intersection multiplicity of the pair computed by
the Tor formula is `1`. Geometrically, for `A` the local ring of a nonsingular variety `X` at the
generic point of an irreducible component `Z` of `V ∩ W`, with `I` and `J` the local ideals of two
closed subvarieties intersecting properly and `Z` of multiplicity one in `V ∩ W`, this says
`e(X, V · W, Z) = 1`. -/
@[stacks 0B1I "the Tor-formula multiplicity, in local form at the generic point"]
theorem localIntersectionMultiplicity_eq_one_of_length_quotient_sup_eq_one {A : Type u}
    [CommRing A] [IsRegularLocalRing A] (I J : Ideal A)
    (hmult : Module.length A (A ⧸ (I ⊔ J)) = 1)
    (hproper : ringKrullDim A ≤ ringKrullDim (A ⧸ I) + ringKrullDim (A ⧸ J)) :
    I.localIntersectionMultiplicity (A ⧸ J) = 1 := by
  classical
  have hterm : ∀ i : ℕ, (-1 : ℚ) ^ i *
      ((Module.length A (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I))).obj
        (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ J)))).toNat : ℚ) = if i = 0 then (1 : ℚ) else 0 := by
    intro i
    rw [length_tor_quotient_of_length_quotient_sup_eq_one I J hmult hproper i]
    by_cases hi : i = 0 <;> simp [hi]
  rw [Ideal.localIntersectionMultiplicity, tsum_congr hterm]
  simp

end IsRegularLocalRing

end
